<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Spescom yr share rises, div up.</title>
<headline>Spescom yr share rises, div up.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended September 30 vs the 17 months ended September</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     31.5     vs   25.1</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  9.0     vs    8.5</p>
<p>    Attrib income	    9.18    vs    5.01</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		    9.62    vs    5.92</p>
<p>    Tax			  0.51    vs    0.62</p>
<p>    Interest paid	    2.45    vs    5.62</p>
<p>    Turnover		 116.73    vs  115.62</p>
<p>Div payable: December 6</p>
<p>on register: January 8</p>
<p>Full name: Spescom Electronics Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Previous results are for the 17 months ended Sept 30 1995 after the company changed its financial year-end.</p>
<p>The company said it would offer capitalisation shares of one cent each in the ratio of one new share for every 100 held.</p>
<p>Prospects for the coming year were encouraging, with earnings growth expected to be in line with Spescom's October 1994 vision of doubling group earnings by the 1997 financial year-end.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
